[color=#ff7700][size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size][/color]
[list=1]
[*][color=#9fc5e8]Locate the following folder in your Octopath Traveler 0 installation:[/color]
[code]Octopath_Traveler0\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods[/code]
[/*]
[*][color=#9fc5e8]Extract the content of the archive into the mods folder[/color][/*]
[*][color=#9fc5e8]Launch the game.[/color][/*]
[/list]
[color=#9fc5e8][color=#ff7700][size=4][b]Notes[/b][/size][/color][/color]
[list]
[*][color=#9fc5e8]Make sure UE4SS is installed and working before using this mod.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#9fc5e8]If the mod does not load, verify the folder name and file placement.[/color][/*]
[/list]
[color=#9fc5e8][color=#ff7700][size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size][/color][/color]
[list]
[*][color=#9fc5e8]The mod can be configured by editing the [b]config.lua[/b] file located in the [b]{ModName}\Scripts[/b] folder.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#9fc5e8]The configuration file contains various settings that can be adjusted to customize the mod's behavior.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#9fc5e8]Refer to the comments within the configuration file for guidance on how to modify the settings.[/color][/*]
[/list]
[color=#9fc5e8][color=#ff7700][size=4][b]Uninstallation[/b][/size][/color][/color]
[list=1]
[*][color=#9fc5e8]Close the game.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#9fc5e8]Remove the [b]{ModName}[/b] folder from[/color]
[code]UE4SS\Mods[/code]
[/*]
[/list]
